<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0061/tu_0001> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "1) High-degree or complete AVB after cardiac surgery A period of clinical observation of at least 5 days is indicated to assess whether the rhythm disturbance is transient and resolves. However, in the case of complete AVB with low or no escape rhythm when resolution is unlikely, this observation period can be shortened.473,478" .
