<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_768e18f1eeabdbc60efa436a98e404979a7b66e6f8b22133183e14bad0dcbfba_n0061/tu_0005> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "5) Patients requiring pacing at the time of tricuspid valve surgery Transvalvular leads should be avoided and epicardial ventricular leads used. During tricuspid valve surgery, removal of pre-existing transvalvular leads should be considered and preferred over sewing in the lead between the annulus and a bioprosthesis or annuloplasty ring. In the case of an isolated tricuspid annuloplasty based on an individual risk–benefit analysis, a pre-existing RV lead may be left in place without jailing it between ring and annulus." .
